Enable the "Darken websites" checkbox in theme settings

Chromium ships kDarkenWebsitesCheckboxInThemesSetting disabled, so the checkbox
never appears and web contents are never auto-darkened. Cromite enables it via
its own cromite_flags/ infrastructure, which this tree does not have, so the
feature default is flipped directly instead.

Effect: Settings > Theme grows a "Darken websites" checkbox, shown only for the
Dark and System default themes. Auto-dark then applies to sites that have no
dark theme of their own, and only while the browser is actually in night mode
(WebContentsDarkModeController.isFeatureEnabled = global setting && inNightMode).
The feature's own kDarkenWebsitesCheckboxOptOut param defaults true, so the
AUTO_DARK_WEB_CONTENT content setting registers as ALLOW: darkening is opt-out
once the feature is on, and can be turned off globally here or per-site from the
app menu.
---
diff --git a/components/content_settings/core/common/features.cc b/components/content_settings/core/common/features.cc
--- a/components/content_settings/core/common/features.cc
+++ b/components/content_settings/core/common/features.cc
@@ -12,7 +12,7 @@ namespace content_settings {
 // Enables auto dark feature in theme settings.
 #if BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID)
 BASE_FEATURE(kDarkenWebsitesCheckboxInThemesSetting,
-             base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
+             base::FEATURE_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
 constexpr base::FeatureParam<bool> kDarkenWebsitesCheckboxOptOut{
     &kDarkenWebsitesCheckboxInThemesSetting, "opt_out", true};
 #endif  // BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID)
